Structural Check
- [S1] STC9 failed: Each branch node must have exactly one incoming and at least two outgoing edges. | Node `b1` has in=1 and out=1. | Node `b3` has in=1 and out=1. | Node `b5` has in=1 and out=1. | DSL: branch(b1,XOR); branch(b3,XOR); branch(b5,XOR)
- [S2] STC11 failed: Each variable definition must have a valid range with at least two distinct values. | Variable `v1` has an invalid range `['Delivery Crew picks-up items at the event site']`. | Variable `v3` has an invalid range `['Customer does not return the missing items']`. | Variable `v5` has an invalid range `['Items are stored for future orders']`.
- [S3] STC15 failed: Every variable used in a guard must be formally defined. | Guard `v1 = 'Delivery Crew picks-up items at the event site'` on `b1 -> n3` uses undefined variable `v1`. | DSL: guard(b1,n3,"v1 = 'Delivery Crew picks-up items at the event site'")
- [S4] STC16 failed: Every outgoing edge of XOR/OR branches must have exactly one guard. | XOR/OR edge `b2 -> c1` has 0 guards; exactly one is required. | XOR/OR edge `b3 -> c1` has 0 guards; exactly one is required. | XOR/OR edge `b4 -> n11` has 0 guards; exactly one is required. | XOR/OR edge `b5 -> n14` has 0 guards; exactly one is required.

Logical Sanity Check
- [L1] LSC1 failed: Every guard must be satisfiable under the declared ranges of its referenced variables. | Guard `v1 = 'Delivery Crew picks-up items at the event site'` on `b1 -> n3` cannot be evaluated: `v1` has no declared range. | DSL: guard(b1,n3,"v1 = 'Delivery Crew picks-up items at the event site'")
- [L2] LSC3 failed: Guards outgoing from XOR/OR branches must cover the whole evaluated state space. | Branch `b1` cannot be evaluated: `v1` has no declared range. | Branch `b2` has no enabled outgoing guard at state [v2=Complete and all items were returned]. | Branch `b4` has no enabled outgoing guard at state [v4=Items can't be repaired and are discarded].
